ing points that way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "South Dakota remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential elections, and the state's underlying partisanship points firmly toward the Republican nominee. The partisan lean gives Republicans an advantage of about fifteen points, and with no incumbent president on the ballot, neither side gains from incumbency. No public general-election polls, expert ratings, or campaign finance figures are available for this race, so the forecast rests almost entirely on the state's partisan lean.\n\nRecent headlines offer little to change that picture. Primary news from South Dakota concerns legislative races, and national coverage focuses on the 2028 primary calendars rather than the general election here. The uncertainty band is wide because direct evidence is thin, but a Democratic win would require a national shift well beyond anything indicated by current reporting. The race is rated Likely Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0482, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0894, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0844, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0865, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0843, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.078, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0834, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0867, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -15.0}, {"da